window.MONSTER_CHUNK_135 = [{"name":"Undead Ooze","cr":6,"xp":2400,"alignment":"NE","size":"Huge","type":"undead","init":-5,"senses":[{"type":"blindsight","modifier":"60 ft."}],"ac":3,"ac_touch":3,"ac_flat_footed":3,"ac_mods":"-5 Dex, -2 size, +0 natural","hp":27,"hd":"6d8","hdvalue":6,"fort":2,"ref":-3,"will":6,"immunities":["cold","ooze traits","undead traits"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":20},{"type":"climb","speed":20}],"melee":"slam +3 (2d4+1 plus 1d6 cold)","space":"15 ft.","reach":"10 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"cold"},{"type":"engulf","details":"DC 15, 1d6 cold"},{"type":"skeletons"}],"strength":12,"dexterity":1,"wisdom":12,"charisma":10,"baseatk":4,"cmb":7,"cmd":12,"cmd_special":"can't be tripped","skills":[{"skill":"Climb","value":9}],"environments":["any underground"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"This creature appears as a large, undulating mass of black goo from which rotted and broken bones protrude.","group":"Ooze","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Engulf","kind":"Ex","details":"The save DC is Strength-based and includes a +1 racial bonus."},{"type":"Skeletons","kind":"Su","details":"As a full-round action, an undead ooze can expel 1d6 skeletons from its mass. Skeletons can act in the round they are expelled, and each skeleton conforms to the basic statistics for its size. Slain skeletons are engulfed by the undead ooze and can be reanimated and expelled again in 1d2 hours. An undead ooze's form holds up to 10 skeletons. These skeletons are included in the determination of the undead ooze's CR."}],"description":"When an ooze moves across the grave of a restless and evil soul, a transformation takes place. The malevolent spirit, still tied to the rotting flesh consumed by the ooze, melds with the ooze. The result is a creature filled with hatred of the living and an intelligence and cunningness not normally known among its kind.\n\nThe undead ooze has an advantage over any other ooze: intelligence. It uses this new gift to its fullest in combat by attacking from surprise or by stalking its prey and attacking when the opportunity presents itself. The undead ooze attacks by slamming its body into its prey. It usually engulfs its foes or expels its skeleton allies to contend with its enemies.","ecology":"","habitat_society":"","credit":"The Undead Ooze originally appeared in Sword & Sorcery Studios' Creature Collection (© Sword & Sorcery Studios, 2000) and is used by permission. It has been modified from the original."},{"name":"Undead Troll","cr":6,"xp":2400,"alignment":"CE","size":"Large","type":"undead","init":2,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"scent"}],"ac":19,"ac_touch":11,"ac_flat_footed":17,"ac_mods":"+2 Dex, +8 natural, -1 size","hp":68,"hd":"8d8+24 (+8)","hdvalue":8,"hp_mods":["fast healing 5"],"fort":5,"ref":4,"will":7,"dr":"5/magic","immunities":["undead traits"],"resists":[{"type":"cold","value":10},{"type":"fire","value":10}],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":40}],"melee":"bite +12 (1d8+7), 2 claws +12 (1d6+7 plus bleed)","space":"10 ft.","reach":"10 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"bleed","details":"1d6"},{"type":"rend","details":"2 claws, 1d6+10"}],"strength":24,"dexterity":14,"intelligence":6,"wisdom":9,"charisma":16,"baseatk":6,"cmb":14,"cmd":26,"feats":[{"feat":"Intimidating Prowess"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Skill Focus (Perception)"},{"feat":"Toughness"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Climb","value":11},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":18},{"skill":"Perception","value":10},{"skill":"Stealth","value":6}],"languages":["Giant"],"environments":["any","cold mountains"],"organizations":["solitary","pair"],"treasure":"standard","description_visual":"This tall and hideous humanoid has sickly green, rotting flesh and hands that end in filthy claws.","group":"Troll","source":"Tome of Horrors 4 (3pp)","description":"Sometimes when a troll dies, the evilness within the creature raises it as an undead troll; a mockery of life and even more evil than it was before (if such is possible). Undead trolls despise all living creatures, especially other trolls. Their sole purpose now seems to be to kill and devour every living thing they encounter. Undeath seems to have cursed them with an eternal hunger, and undead trolls are forever seeking to satiate their appetite. Undead trolls don't eat other undead trolls however. Though they tend to inhabit the same cold mountains they did in life, undead trolls can be found anywhere.\n\nUndead trolls generally resemble normal trolls in stature. Their flesh has taken on a sickly green appearance and is rotting in various places. Their teeth and nails are filthy and these creatures are almost always caked in dried blood.\n\nUndead trolls are relentless in combat, always fighting to the death. They attack as do standard trolls, using wicked claws and bites. While they lack the true regenerative powers of a standard troll, their ability to quickly heal still complicates combat for a lot of would-be troll slayers.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Vegepygmy Chief","cr":6,"xp":2400,"alignment":"N","size":"Medium","type":"plant","subtypes":["fungus"],"init":1,"senses":[{"type":"low-light vision"}],"ac":17,"ac_touch":11,"ac_flat_footed":16,"ac_mods":"+1 Dex, +6 natural","hp":76,"hd":"9d8+36","hdvalue":9,"fort":9,"ref":4,"will":5,"dr":"5/bludgeoning or slashing","immunities":["electricity","plant traits"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":30}],"melee":"2 claws +11 (1d6+5) or mwk spear +13 (1d8+7/x3)","ranged":"mwk spear +9 (1d8+5/x3)","space":"5 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"spores"}],"strength":21,"dexterity":12,"constitution":17,"intelligence":12,"wisdom":15,"charisma":16,"baseatk":6,"cmb":11,"cmd":22,"feats":[{"feat":"Cleave"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Skill Focus (Perception)"},{"feat":"Toughness"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (spear)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Diplomacy","value":4},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":8},{"skill":"Perception","value":17},{"skill":"Stealth","value":17,"special":"+25 in forested or swampy areas"},{"skill":"Survival","value":5}],"environments":["any underground"],"organizations":["band (1 plus 1 subchief, 2-8 bodyguards, 4-7 guards, 6-10 workers)","tribe (30-300 commoners plus 2-8 guards, 2-8 bodyguards, 1 subchief per 50 commoners, 1 chief per 100 commoners, 10-24 thornies, 1-4 patches of russet mold, 1-3 shriekers)"],"treasure":"standard","description_visual":"This creature resembles a humanoid with green vegetable-like skin and razor-sharp claws. Its head sports two large yellow eyes, a wide mouth, inset nose, and a topknot of dark brown leaves. Leafy tendrils protrude from its shoulders, midsection, arms, and legs.","group":"Vegepygmy","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Spores","kind":"Ex","details":"The chief is the only vegepygmy with a spore attack. As a standard action, a chief vegepygmy can release a cloud of spores in a 40-foot spread. A living creature caught within the cloud must succeed on a DC 17 Fortitude save or be paralyzed for 2d6 rounds. After the paralysis wears off, the character must succeed on another DC 17 Fortitude save or take 3d6 points of Constitution damage. This save DC is Constitution-based. At Constitution 0 a creature dies, and rises as a 4 HD vegepygmy bodyguard in one day. If a remove disease spell is cast on a paralyzed victim before the paralysis wears off, he doesn't have to attempt the second Fortitude save and takes no Constitution damage."}],"description":"When a living creature is slain by russet mold (see that entry), it rises as a vegepygmy commoner. Vegepygmies are low-intelligence plants that make their home deep in the forests or underground away from most settled areas. They are hunters and scavengers, and carnivorous, preying on living creatures weaker than themselves. A vegepygmy ranges from two ft. to four and a half ft. tall. Though they don't seem to have ears, it is well known that vegepygmies can hear. Vegepygmies don't speak, but communicate with others of their kind by thumping their chest or rapping their spears on rocks, earth, or some other solid surface. It isn't known if or how they communicate with other creatures. Vegepygmies attack with claws or weapons, usually either a longspear or club. They prefer to ambush opponents, using their coloration to blend with their natural surroundings.","ecology":"","habitat_society":"","credit":"The Vegepygmy originally appeared in the First Edition module S3 Expedition to the Barrier Peaks (© TSR/Wizards of the Coast, 1980) and later in the First Edition Monster Manual II (© TSR/Wizards of the Coast, 1983) and is used by permission.","gear":"masterwork spear"},{"name":"White Pudding","cr":6,"xp":2400,"alignment":"N","size":"Huge","type":"ooze","init":-5,"senses":[{"type":"blindsight","modifier":"60 ft."}],"ac":3,"ac_touch":3,"ac_flat_footed":3,"ac_mods":"-5 Dex, -2 size, +0 natural","hp":94,"hd":"9d8+54","hdvalue":9,"fort":8,"ref":-2,"will":-2,"defensive_abilities":["split (piercing and slashing, 10 hp)"],"immunities":["ooze traits"],"resists":[{"type":"cold","value":5}],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":20},{"type":"climb","speed":20}],"melee":"slam +7 (2d6+4 plus 2d6 acid plus grab)","space":"15 ft.","reach":"10 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"constrict","details":"2d6+4 plus 2d6 acid"},{"type":"corrosion"}],"strength":17,"dexterity":1,"constitution":21,"wisdom":1,"charisma":1,"baseatk":6,"cmb":11,"cmb_special":"+4 vs. grapple","cmd":16,"cmd_special":"+10 vs. bull rush, can't be tripped","skills":[{"skill":"Climb","value":11}],"sq":[{"type":"camouflage"},{"type":"suction"}],"environments":["cold plains","cold underground"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"A glistening white sheet of snow and ice moves across the area.","group":"Pudding","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Acid","kind":"Ex","details":"A white pudding secretes a digestive acid that dissolves organic material quickly, but doesn't affect metal or stone. Any melee hit or constriction attack deals acid damage, and the opponent's clothing and armor (non-metal only) take the same amount of damage unless they succeed on DC 19 Reflex saves. A wooden weapon that strikes a white pudding takes 2d6 acid damage unless it succeeds on a DC 19 Reflex save. If a white pudding remains in contact with a wooden object for 1 full round, it inflicts 19 points of damage (no save) to the object. The save DCs are Constitution-based."},{"type":"Camouflage","kind":"Ex","details":"Since a white pudding looks like normal ice and snow when at rest, it takes a DC 20 Perception check to notice it before it attacks. Anyone with ranks in Survival or Knowledge (nature) can use one of those skills instead of Perception to notice the white pudding. Dwarves can use stonecunning to notice a subterranean-dwelling white pudding."},{"type":"Corrosion","kind":"Ex","details":"An opponent that is being constricted by a white pudding suffers a -4 penalty on Reflex saves made to resist acid damage applying to clothing and armor."},{"type":"Suction","kind":"Ex","details":"The white pudding can create powerful suction against any surfaces as it climbs, allowing it to cling to inverted surfaces with ease. A white pudding can establish or release suction as a swift action, and as long as it is using suction, it moves at half speed. Because of the suction, a white pudding's CMD score gets a +10 circumstance bonus to resist bull rush, awesome blows, and other attacks and effects that attempt to physically move it from its location."}],"description":"A variety of the black pudding, the white pudding is found only in cold, frigid lands. It is white in color and uses this to its advantage by ambushing its prey.\n\nWhite puddings attack by grabbing and constricting their prey. A white pudding waits motionless for its prey to move within range before striking.","ecology":"","habitat_society":"","credit":"The White Pudding originally appeared in the First Edition module S4 Lost Caverns of Tsojcanth (© TSR/Wizards of the Coast, 1982) and later in the First Edition Monster Manual II (© TSR/Wizards of the Coast, 1983) and is used by permission."},{"name":"Wood Golem","cr":6,"xp":2400,"alignment":"N","size":"Medium","type":"construct","init":-1,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"low-light vision"}],"ac":19,"ac_touch":9,"ac_flat_footed":19,"ac_mods":"-1 Dex, +10 natural","hp":64,"hd":"8d10+20","hdvalue":8,"fort":2,"ref":1,"will":2,"dr":"5/adamantine","immunities":["cold","construct traits","electricity"],"weaknesses":["vulnerability to fire"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":30}],"melee":"2 slams +13 (1d8+5)","space":"5 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","strength":20,"dexterity":9,"wisdom":11,"charisma":1,"baseatk":8,"cmb":13,"cmd":22,"sq":[{"type":"alarm"}],"environments":["any"],"organizations":["solitary","gang (2-5)"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"This automaton is human-sized and resembles a ornately carved wooden statue.","group":"Golem","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Alarm","kind":"Sp","details":"The golem lets out a piercing howl that lasts for 6 rounds when anyone other than its creator enters the area it is guarding (or comes within 50 ft. of the golem). This functions similar to the audible version of the alarm spell and can be heard to a range of 100 ft."}],"description":"Arcane spellcasters used several ancient texts to arrive at a process to create inexpensive yet still quite powerful golems. They had master craftsmen create wood statues with articulating limbs and then performed the proper spells to animate and control them. The statues vary in shape and form and usually have weapons of some sort held in each hand. The wood golems were designed to act both as an alarm and a protection against intruders. Wood golems are usually programmed to close doors and avoid ranged weapons and spells but don't break off melee combat to avoid missile fire from other sources. They attack with their fists. Construction The pieces of a wood golem are assembled from blocks of fine wood and sprinkled with rare powders and crushed herbs worth at least 300 gp. WOOD GOLEM CL 12th; Price 16,550 gp Requirements Craft Construct, alarm, animate objects, geas/quest, limited wish, resist energy (cold, electricity), creator must be caster level 12th; Skill Craft (carpentry) DC 17; Cost 8,425 gp","ecology":"","habitat_society":"","credit":"Wood Golems originally appeared in the Necromancer Games adventure Hall of the Rainbow Mage."},{"name":"Young Gray Dragon","cr":6,"xp":2400,"alignment":"NE","size":"Medium","type":"dragon","subtypes":["water"],"init":6,"senses":[{"type":"dragon senses"}],"ac":22,"ac_touch":12,"ac_flat_footed":20,"ac_mods":"+2 Dex, +10 natural","hp":66,"hd":"7d12+21","hdvalue":7,"fort":8,"ref":9,"will":6,"immunities":["paralysis","sleep"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":60},{"type":"fly","speed":150,"maneuverability":"average"},{"type":"swim","speed":40}],"melee":"2 claws +11 (1d6+4), bite +11 (1d8+6), 2 wings +11 (1d4+2)","space":"5 ft.","reach":"5 ft. (10 ft. with bite)","special_attacks":[{"type":"breath weapon","details":"60-ft. line, 6d6 fire; DC 16 Ref half"}],"strength":19,"dexterity":14,"constitution":17,"intelligence":11,"wisdom":13,"charisma":11,"baseatk":7,"cmb":11,"cmd":23,"cmd_special":"+4 vs. trip","feats":[{"feat":"Alertness"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Lightning Reflexes"},{"feat":"Multiattack"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Bluff","value":10},{"skill":"Fly","value":12},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":10},{"skill":"Knowledge (local)","value":8},{"skill":"Perception","value":13},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":3},{"skill":"Stealth","value":12},{"skill":"Swim","value":17}],"languages":["Draconic Special Abilities"],"environments":["warm coastlines"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"triple standard","description_visual":"Steam emanates from the nostrils and mouth of this slate gray dragon.","group":"Dragon","source":"Tome of Horrors 4 (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Breath Weapon","kind":"Su","details":"A gray dragon's breath weapon is a superheated line of steam."},{"type":"Change Shape","kind":"Su","details":"A young or older gray dragon can take any animal or humanoid form 3/day as if using polymorph."},{"type":"Corrupt Water","kind":"Sp","details":"Once per day an adult or older gray dragon can stagnate 10 cubic ft. of still water, making it foul and unable to support water-breathing life. The ability spoils liquids containing water. Liquid-based magic items (such as potions) and items in a creature's possession must succeed on a Will save (DC 19) or become ruined. This ability is the equivalent of a 1st-level spell. Its range is 180 ft."},{"type":"Spell-Like Abilities","kind":"Sp","details":"A gray dragon gains the following spell-like abilities, usable at will upon reaching the listed age category. • Young-fog cloud; • Juvenile-create water; • Old-control winds; • Ancient-control water;"},{"type":"Water Breathing","kind":"Ex","details":"A gray dragon breathes water and can use its breath weapon, spells, and abilities underwater."}],"description":"Gray dragons are evil dragons that inhabit mountains and hills near coastlines. They have little regard for other races and often enslave others to do their bidding. Adult and older gray dragons are rarely found without a retinue of humanoid slaves. Gray dragons mate for life and a single mated pair often terrorizes nearby villages, laying waste to those that oppose the dragon's will.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Abasheen Genie","cr":7,"xp":3200,"alignment":"N","size":"Large","type":"outsider","subtypes":["air","extraplanar"],"init":7,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."}],"ac":21,"ac_touch":13,"ac_flat_footed":17,"ac_mods":"+3 Dex, +1 dodge, +8 natural, -1 size","hp":85,"hd":"10d10+30","hdvalue":10,"fort":6,"ref":12,"will":13,"defensive_abilities":["air mastery"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":20},{"type":"fly","speed":50,"maneuverability":"perfect"}],"melee":"2 slams +12 (2d6+3) or masterwork falchion +13  (2d6+3/18-20)","space":"10 ft.","reach":"10 ft.","spell_like_abilities_caster_level":10,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":17,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"charm person"},{"spell":"command"},{"spell":"plane shift","details":"willing targets to elemental planes, Astral Plane, or Material Plane only"}]},{"frequency":"1/day","spells":[{"spell":"geas/quest"}]}],"strength":16,"dexterity":17,"constitution":16,"intelligence":20,"wisdom":18,"charisma":17,"baseatk":10,"cmb":14,"cmd":28,"feats":[{"feat":"Combat Casting"},{"feat":"Dodge"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Lightning Reflexes"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Bluff","value":16},{"skill":"Diplomacy","value":16},{"skill":"Fly","value":22},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":16},{"skill":"Knowledge (arcana)","value":18},{"skill":"Knowledge (nobility)","value":18},{"skill":"Knowledge (planes)","value":18},{"skill":"Perception","value":17},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":17},{"skill":"Spellcraft","value":15},{"skill":"Use Magic Device","value":13}],"languages":["Abyssal","Auran","Common","Celestial","Infernal","telepathy 100 ft."],"environments":["any (Elemental Plane of Air)"],"organizations":["solitary","pair","company (2-5)"],"treasure":"standard","description_visual":"This being stands 8 ft. tall in flowing robes of purple and gold. Its hair is black and tied back in a ponytail with a ribbon of gold.","group":"Genie","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Air Mastery","kind":"Ex","details":"Airborne creatures take a -1 penalty on attack and damage rolls against an abasheen."}],"description":"Abasheens are genies from the Plane of Air and serve the nobles of that plane as diplomats, couriers, and emissaries. Some of the less scrupulous serve as spies and insurgents. They are extremely clever and often let their arrogance interfere with their assignments. Abasheen look down on all creatures from the Material Plane.\n\nAbasheens and common djinn tolerate each other, but that is as far as it goes. They rarely work together and when they do, such pairings often degenerate into quarrels. The society structure of the abasheen is unknown but it is believed to be vastly different than that of the other genies. No abasheen nobles are known to exist and the entire race seems to be servitor to the race of djinn.\n\nAn abasheen stands about 8 ft. tall and is always dressed in flowing robes colored to denote their current station. Their skin is dark and their build powerful. All have dark hair, either black or brown, and most wear their hair braided or pulled into a ponytail, tied with ribbons of gold or silver.\n\nAbasheens rely on their physical attack and spell-like abilities in combat. When combat starts, an abasheen commands one of its opponents (usually the one closest to it) to drop or flee (see the command spell).\n\nOn its next action it either bashes an opponent with its fists (if one is close enough) or attempts to charm an enemy spellcaster.\n\nDuring combat, an abasheen rarely touches the ground, preferring to remain airborne and above its opponents. They rarely fight to the death. Should combat turn against an abasheen it always attempts to escape, usually by plane shifting away.","ecology":"","habitat_society":"","gear":"masterwork falchion"},{"name":"Abyssal Wolf","cr":7,"xp":3200,"alignment":"CE","size":"Large","type":"magical beast","subtypes":["chaotic","evil","extraplanar"],"init":7,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"keen scent"},{"type":"know alignment"},{"type":"low-light vision"}],"ac":20,"ac_touch":12,"ac_flat_footed":17,"ac_mods":"+3 Dex, +8 natural, -1 size","hp":80,"hd":"7d10+42","hdvalue":7,"fort":10,"ref":8,"will":6,"dr":"10/cold iron","sr":18,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":50}],"melee":"bite +11 (1d8+7 plus trip)","space":"10 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"paralyzing gaze"}],"strength":20,"dexterity":17,"constitution":20,"intelligence":8,"wisdom":14,"charisma":17,"baseatk":7,"cmb":13,"cmd":26,"cmd_special":"+4 vs. trip","feats":[{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Toughness"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Perception","value":9,"special":"+11 vs. half-fiends and tieflings"},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":2,"special":"+4 vs. half-fiends and tieflings"},{"skill":"Stealth","value":5}],"languages":["Abyssal","Common"],"environments":["any Abyss"],"organizations":["solitary","pair","pack (4-11)"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"This creature is a man-sized wolf with deep blackish-blue fur and fiery orange eyes. Its coat is caked with blood, and bits of flesh hang from its toothy maw.","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Keen Scent","kind":"Ex","details":"An abyssal wolf can detect prey within 60 ft. by sense of smell, as per the scent ability. This range increases to 120 ft. if the opponents are upwind; and decreases to 30 ft. if downwind. By making a successful DC 15 Wisdom check the abyssal wolf can determine whether a tiefling or half-fiend is present among the opponents."},{"type":"Know Alignment","kind":"Su","details":"Abyssal wolves always know the alignment of any creature they look upon. This ability can be negated or dispelled, but the abyssal wolf can activate it again as a free action on its next turn."},{"type":"Paralyzing Gaze","kind":"Su","details":"Anyone within 40 ft. meeting the gaze of an abyssal wolf must make a successful DC 16 Will save or be paralyzed for 2d4 rounds. Half-fiends and tieflings have a -2 circumstance penalty on this save. Once a successful save is made, the target is immune to the effects of that abyssal wolf's gaze attack for one day. The save DC is Charisma-based."}],"description":"Abyssal wolves roam the Abyss seeking sources of meat. They savor the flesh and blood of lesser demons and have a particular liking for the taste of tieflings and good-aligned outsiders. Should a pack of abyssal wolves run across one of the aforementioned creatures, it doesn't hesitate to attack. The blood and flesh of half-fiends is another meal that these monsters enjoy, so they rarely turn down an opportunity to hunt on the Material Plane. Many demon lords find it blasphemous that their own kind mate with mortals, and thus unleash these monsters on the Material Plane to deal with such creatures. Most often when encountered on the Material Plane, abyssal wolves have either been summoned by an evil spellcaster or unleashed by one of the demonic lords of the Abyss.\n\nThe abyssal wolf is a man-sized wolf that stands 5 ft. tall at the shoulder. When enraged, the hair on the nape of its neck stands up and the wolf issues forth a low growl, bearing its razor-sharp (and usually blood-stained) teeth.\n\nAbyssal wolves hunt in packs. When prey is sighted, the monsters move within range where they can use their paralyzing gaze. Foes that are not paralyzed are dealt with first; the wolves circle an opponent and take turns charging in and attacking. A foe that is tripped is pounced on by the pack. Once the pack deals with the immediate threat, they turn their attention to any paralyzed creatures and tear them to pieces.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Algant","cr":7,"xp":3200,"alignment":"NG","size":"Huge","type":"plant","subtypes":["aquatic"],"init":2,"senses":[{"type":"blindsense","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"tremorsense","modifier":"120 ft."}],"ac":20,"ac_touch":10,"ac_flat_footed":18,"ac_mods":"+2 Dex, +10 natural, -2 size","hp":95,"hd":"10d8+50","hdvalue":10,"fort":12,"ref":5,"will":3,"dr":"10/slashing","immunities":["plant traits"],"weaknesses":["vulnerability to fire"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":10},{"type":"swim","speed":30}],"melee":"slam +12 (2d6+10/19-20 plus grab)","space":"15 ft.","reach":"10 ft.","strength":25,"dexterity":14,"constitution":21,"intelligence":12,"wisdom":15,"charisma":12,"baseatk":7,"cmb":7,"cmd":17,"feats":[{"feat":"Alertness"},{"feat":"Endurance"},{"feat":"Improved Critical (slam)","type":"bonus"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Swim-By Attack"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Diplomacy","value":7},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":7},{"skill":"Knowledge (nature)","value":7},{"skill":"Perception","value":11},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":8},{"skill":"Stealth","value":1,"special":"+17 in native environs"},{"skill":"Swim","value":15}],"languages":["Algant","Aquan","Common"],"sq":[{"type":"amphibious"},{"type":"animate plants"},{"type":"double damage against objects"},{"type":"plantspeech"}],"environments":["any water (freshwater)"],"organizations":["solitary","patch (2-7)"],"treasure":"standard","description_visual":"A large tentacle rises from this gigantic mass of seaweed.","group":"Plant Guardian","source":"Tome of Horrors 4 (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Engulf","kind":"Ex","details":"An algant can simply engulf Huge or smaller creatures in its path as a standard action. It cannot make a slam attack during the round in which it engulfs. The algant merely has to move over the opponents, affecting as many as it can cover. Opponents can make attacks of opportunity against the creature, but if they do so they are not entitled to a saving throw. Those who don't attempt attacks of opportunity can attempt a DC 22 Reflex save to avoid being engulfed-in a success, they are pushed back or aside (opponent's choice) as the creature moves forward. Engulfed creatures are subject to an automatic slam attack each round, gain the pinned condition, are in danger of drowning, and are trapped within the algant's body until they are no longer pinned. The save DC is Strength-based."},{"type":"Animate Plants","kind":"Sp","details":"A plant guardian can animate any plants of the same type within 180 ft. at will, controlling up to two such plants at a time. It takes 1 full round for the plant to uproot itself, after which it moves at a speed of 10 ft. and fights as a plant of the same type as the one animating it (exceptions are noted in each entry below), gaining the plant guardian's vulnerability to fire. If the plant guardian that animated it terminates the animation, moves out of range, or is incapacitated, the plant immediately takes root wherever it is and returns to its normal state."},{"type":"Double Damage against Objects","kind":"Ex","details":"A plant guardian or animated tree that makes a full attack against an object or structure deals double damage."},{"type":"Plantspeech","kind":"Ex","details":"A plant guardian has the ability to converse with plants as if subject to a continual speak with plants spell, and most plants greet them with an attitude of friendly or helpful."}],"description":"The algants are the plant guardians of the water. An algant resembles a large mass of algae and dwells in freshwater.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Apparition","cr":7,"xp":3200,"alignment":"CE","size":"Medium","type":"undead","subtypes":["incorporeal"],"init":6,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"lifesense"}],"auras":["unnatural aura (30 ft.)"],"ac":15,"ac_touch":15,"ac_flat_footed":13,"ac_mods":"+2 Dex, +3 deflection","hp":52,"hd":"7d8+21","hdvalue":7,"fort":5,"ref":4,"will":8,"defensive_abilities":["incorporeal","channel resistance +2"],"immunities":["undead traits"],"weaknesses":["resurrection vulnerability","sunlight powerlessness"],"speed":[{"type":"fly","speed":60,"maneuverability":"perfect"}],"space":"5 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"create spawn"},{"type":"spectral strangulation"}],"dexterity":14,"intelligence":10,"wisdom":13,"charisma":16,"baseatk":5,"cmb":7,"cmd":20,"feats":[{"feat":"Blind-Fight"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Skill Focus (Perception)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Fly","value":10},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":13},{"skill":"Knowledge (religion)","value":10},{"skill":"Perception","value":14},{"skill":"Stealth","value":12}],"environments":["any"],"organizations":["solitary","gang (2-4)"],"treasure":"standard","description_visual":"This translucent and skeletal creature is clothed in tattered rags. Its eyes burn with a crimson light.","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Create Spawn","kind":"Su","details":"A humanoid slain by an apparition becomes an apparition itself in 1d4 rounds. Spawn so created are less powerful than typical apparitions, and suffer a -2 penalty on all d20 rolls and checks. They also receive -2 hp per HD, and a -2 penalty to the Will save DC of their spectral strangulation ability. Spawn are under the command of the apparition that created them and remain enslaved until its death, at which point they lose their spawn penalties and become full-fledged and free-willed apparitions. They don't possess any of the abilities they had in life."},{"type":"Resurrection Vulnerability","kind":"Su","details":"A raise dead or similar spell cast on an apparition destroys it (Will negates). Using the spell in this way doesn't require a material component."},{"type":"Spectral Strangulation","kind":"Su","details":"An apparition attacks an opponent by implanting a suggestion in the victim's mind, convincing it that it is being strangled by the apparition's bony claws. The apparition must be on the same plane as the target creature to use this ability. The target of the spectral strangulation feels the bony, claw-like fingers of the apparition at its throat-even through armor. The target must succeed on a DC 16 Will save to disbelieve the suggestion. A creature that successfully saves cannot be affected again by the same apparition's suggestion for one day. On a failed save, the victim must immediately succeed on a DC 16 Fortitude save or die from fright due to heart failure. If the Fortitude save succeeds, the victim acts as if affected by a fear spell for 1d4 rounds. A creature protected by magic circle against evil or protection from evil cannot be affected by an apparition's spectral strangulation. This is a mind-affecting fear effect. The save DCs are Charisma-based."},{"type":"Sunlight Powerlessness","kind":"Ex","details":"Apparitions on the Material Plane are utterly powerless in natural sunlight (not merely a daylight spell) and flee from it. An apparition caught in sunlight cannot attack and is staggered."},{"type":"Unnatural Aura","kind":"Su","details":"Animals don't willingly approach the creature unless the animal's master succeeds at a DC 25 Handle Animal, Ride, or wild empathy check.."}],"description":"Apparitions are undead spirits of creatures that died as the result of an accident. The twist of fate that ended their life prematurely has driven them totally and completely to the side of evil. An apparition is often mistaken for a ghost or spectre. Apparitions hate all living creatures and attack them on sight. Apparitions are ethereal creatures and they exist mainly on the Ethereal Plane.\n\nAn apparition looks much like it did in life.\n\nAn apparition has no physical attacks and attacks by fear alone. By implanting a suggestion in a victim's mind, it attempts to actually scare the life out of its opponent. Once the apparition selects a target, it uses its spectral strangulation ability. If overpowered or if it fails in its attempt to slay a living creature, the apparition flees back to the Ethereal Plane.","ecology":"","habitat_society":"","credit":"The Apparition originally appeared in the First Edition Fiend Folio (© TSR/Wizards of the Coast, 1981) and is used by permission."},{"name":"Arach","cr":7,"xp":3200,"alignment":"NE","size":"Medium","type":"monstrous humanoid","init":7,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."}],"ac":19,"ac_touch":13,"ac_flat_footed":16,"ac_mods":"+3 Dex, +6 natural","hp":76,"hd":"9d10+27","hdvalue":9,"fort":6,"ref":9,"will":9,"defensive_abilities":["spider passivism"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":30},{"type":"climb","speed":10}],"melee":"bite +12 (1d6+2), 6 slams +12 (1d4+2), or short sword +12 (1d6+2) and 5 short swords +12 (1d6+2), bite +7 (1d6+1 plus poison)","space":"5 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"multispell"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":9,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":12,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"2/day","spells":[{"spell":"summon","details":"level 4, 9 HD of monstrous spiders, 100%"}]}],"strength":15,"dexterity":17,"constitution":16,"intelligence":10,"wisdom":12,"charisma":12,"baseatk":9,"cmb":11,"cmd":24,"feats":[{"feat":"Blind-Fight"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Multiweapon Fighting"},{"feat":"Weapon Finesse"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Climb","value":17},{"skill":"Craft (weaving)","value":7},{"skill":"Knowledge (dungeoneering)","value":9},{"skill":"Perception","value":18},{"skill":"Stealth","value":19}],"languages":["Common","Undercommon"],"environments":["any underground"],"organizations":["solitary","pair","nest (6-11 plus 3-6 Medium or Small monstrous spiders)"],"treasure":"standard","description_visual":"This six-armed humanoid has a lithe build and stands just under sevenft. tall. It has a narrow aquiline face and bony plates protruding from its thorax and limbs.","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Multispell","kind":"Ex","details":"An arach spellcaster (one that has taken levels in a spellcasting class) can cast multiple spells in a given round. If each spell is 3rd-level or less, an arach can cast up to three spells per round; 4th- or 5th-level spells, two per round. An arach cannot multispell spells higher than 5th-level."},{"type":"Poison","kind":"Ex","details":"Arach Venom: Bite-injury; save Fort DC 17; frequency 1/round for 4 rounds; effect 1d4 Str; cure 1 save. An arach can also coat a single weapon it wields with this poison as a move action. The save DC is Constitution-based."},{"type":"Spider Passivism","kind":"Ex","details":"No spiders, monstrous spiders, phase spiders, temporal crawlers, sand stalkers, arachnid werecreatures (such as werespiders) or other spider-like creatures with an Intelligence of 8 or less willingly attack an arach. They can be forced to do so through magical means however. If the arach or one of its allies attacks the creature first, this passivism is negated for that creature for 24 hours."}],"description":"Arachs are a strange union of sentient arachnids and humanoids. With the exception of their heads, they are completely hairless, and their skin ranges from glossy brown to grey and pitch black with white plates on the males and red plates on the females. Many believe they were once worshippers of the spider god who long ago were granted this horrid transformation. Arachs live in small colonies (called nests among their own kind) in caves and caverns deep underground. They generally shun other subterranean races preferring to keep company with their own kind. Occasionally an arach nest makes an alliance with a band of driders though such a union is usually short-lived (the races get along, but don't particularly like each other for unknown reasons). A nest is led by the most powerful spellcaster among the members, usually a sorcerer or wizard of at least 7th level. Arach nests include an equal number of male and female members. Both forage and hunt for the nest, and in times of battle, both fight to defend the lair. During mating season, females are less active as they await the birth of their young. Young are always born live and a typical female spawns 1d4 young at one time. Young arachs reach maturity after 6 years. An arach stands about 6 to 6-1/2 ft. tall and weighs about 200 pounds. Arach spellcasters open with a whirlwind of blows from their swordwielding arms. Arach fighters either opt for multiple blows from their short swords, or wield two large weapons or polearms with no penalty for off handed attacks due to their use of three arms to balance and attack. An arach spellbinder opens combat with a lightning bolt or touch of idiocy (if an opponent is within range). It follows this with a magic missile assault and then continues the battle mixing sword attacks and spell attacks. All arachs summon spiders in the first round of combat if possible to absorb larger numbers of enemies or quickly overwhelm smaller numbers of foes.","as_character":[{"description":"Arachs have racial Hit Dice and can have class levels. Most arachs are sorcerers or wizards. Arach clerics tend to worship gods of magic and spiders, and can choose two of the following domains: Darkness, Magic, Arach characters possess the following racial traits.","racial_traits":[{"type":"Ability Score Bonuses","value":"+4 Strength, +6 Dexterity, +6 Constitution, +2 Wisdom, +2 Charisma: Arachs are strong, quick, disciplined and confident."},{"type":"Base Speed","value":"Arachs' base speed is 30 ft. An arach has a climb speed of 10 ft."},{"type":"Darkvision","value":"Arachs can see in the dark up to 60 ft."},{"type":"Racial Hit Dice","value":"An arach begins with nine levels of monstrous humanoid, which provide 9d10 Hit Dice, a base attack bonus of +9, base saves of Fort +3, Ref +6, and Will +6."},{"type":"Racial Skills","value":"An arach's monstrous humanoid levels give it skill points equal to 9 x (4 + Int modifier, minimum 1). Arachs have a +4 racial bonus on Perception and Stealth skill checks."},{"type":"Racial Feats","value":"An arach's monstrous humanoid levels give it five feats."},{"type":"AC","value":"+6 natural armor bonus Natural Weapons: An arch can fight with six slams (1d4) or one-handed weapons and a bite (1d6)."},{"type":"Special Attacks","value":"multispell, poision, summon spiders SQ: spider passivism"},{"type":"Languages","value":"Arachs begin play speaking Common and Undercommon. Arachs with high Intelligence scores can choose from among the following bonus languages: Draconic, Giant, Goblin, Terran."}]}],"ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Arcanoplasm","cr":7,"xp":3200,"alignment":"N","size":"Large","type":"aberration","init":4,"senses":[{"type":"arcanesense"},{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."}],"ac":16,"ac_touch":9,"ac_flat_footed":16,"ac_mods":"+7 natural, -1 size","hp":73,"hd":"7d8+42","hdvalue":7,"fort":8,"ref":2,"will":7,"defensive_abilities":["absorb arcane energy","amorphous"],"immunities":["paralysis","poison","polymorph","sleep effects","stunning"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":30},{"type":"climb","speed":10}],"melee":"slam +7 (2d4+3 plus 1d6 acid plus grab)","space":"10 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"arcane spell mimicry"},{"type":"constrict","details":"2d4+3 plus 1d6 acid"}],"strength":15,"dexterity":11,"constitution":22,"intelligence":10,"wisdom":14,"charisma":14,"baseatk":5,"cmb":8,"cmd":18,"cmd_special":"can't be tripped","feats":[{"feat":"Ability Focus (arcane spell mimicry)"},{"feat":"Combat Casting"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (slam)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Climb","value":20},{"skill":"Perception","value":12},{"skill":"Spellcraft","value":18},{"skill":"Stealth","value":7}],"languages":["understands Common and Draconic (cannot speak)"],"environments":["any underground"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"This creature resembles a giant, pale amoeba shot through with stripes of dark gray. Caught within its protoplasmic form are half-digested creatures of various types and sizes.","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Absorb Arcane Energy","kind":"Su","details":"Any arcane spell targeted at an arcanoplasm is automatically absorbed into its body. This cures 1 point of damage per 3 points of damage the spell would otherwise deal (non-damaging spells cure 1 point of damage per spell level). Spells that affect an area are not absorbed, but neither do they affect the arcanoplasm. The arcanoplasm cannot absorb divine magic and is affected normally by such magic."},{"type":"Acid","kind":"Ex","details":"An arcanoplasm secretes a highly corrosive acid that dissolves only flesh."},{"type":"Arcane Spell Mimicry","kind":"Su","details":"An arcanoplasm can mimic any arcane spell cast within 30 ft. of it on its next turn. The spell takes effect as if cast by a 7th-level sorcerer (save DC 14 + spell level) and doesn't require any components. The arcanoplasm cannot mimic spells a 7th-level arcane caster could not normally cast (i.e., it cannot mimic divine spells, or arcane spells of 5th level or higher). The save DC is Charisma-based. Due to their innately magical nature, an arcanoplasm adds its Constitution modifier in addition to its Charisma modifier to all concentration checks to cast a spell using arcane spell mimicry."},{"type":"Arcanesense","kind":"Su","details":"An arcanoplasm can automatically detect the location of any arcane spellcaster within 100 ft. This functions like blindsense but isn't blocked by stone, lead, or other material, and can only sense the location of arcane spellcasters Thought to be the result of a failed magic experiment, wizards and sorcerers alike have tried for years to gather information on this alien creature, but thus far such information has eluded even the most resourceful of casters."}],"description":"Arcanoplasms are found in areas where the residual energies of arcane magic linger. Such areas include ruined wizard towers, keeps, dungeons, and so forth. Here they feed and remain until disturbed. Most encounters with these monsters are take place in such locations as the arcanoplasm rarely travels far from its lair. And since it lairs in ruins and other such adventurer-attracting places, it rarely has to wait long between meals. Arcanoplasms always target arcane spellcasting creatures first. Their innate ability to detect such creatures allows them to do so with precision accuracy. Because of its ability to replicate spells cast near it, the arcanoplasm always tries to stay within 30 ft. of an arcane caster. Mimicked spells are cast at the foe deemed most threatening. Note that because an arcanoplasm's arcane spell mimicry is a supernatural ability and not actual spellcasting, it cannot absorb arcane energy from spells it casts itself.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Black Troll","cr":7,"xp":3200,"alignment":"CE","size":"Large","type":"humanoid","subtypes":["giant"],"init":1,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"low-light vision"},{"type":"scent"}],"ac":18,"ac_touch":10,"ac_flat_footed":17,"ac_mods":"+1 Dex, +8 natural, -1 size","hp":84,"hd":"8d8+48","hdvalue":8,"hp_mods":["regeneration 5 (acid or cold)"],"fort":12,"ref":3,"will":3,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":30}],"melee":"bite +12 (1d8+7), 2 claws +13 (1d6+7)","space":"10 ft.","reach":"10 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"rend","details":"2 claws, 1d6+9"}],"strength":24,"dexterity":12,"constitution":23,"intelligence":5,"wisdom":9,"charisma":6,"baseatk":6,"cmb":14,"cmd":25,"feats":[{"feat":"Intimidating Prowess"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Skill Focus (Perception)"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (claw)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Climb","value":12},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":11},{"skill":"Perception","value":8}],"languages":["Giant"],"environments":["cold mountains"],"organizations":["solitary","gang (1-2 plus 2-5 trolls)"],"treasure":"standard","description_visual":"This tall, grotesque creature has a shiny black hide and hands that end in wicked claws. Two large tusks protrude from its fang-filled mouth.","group":"Troll","source":"Tome of Horrors 4 (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Fire Absorption","kind":"Su","details":"Any fire effect that would deal 20 or more points of damage to a fire troll causes the creature to grow to Huge size. A black troll can induce this effect itself by stepping into a large source of fire that deals 20 or more points of damage in a single round. It must spend one full round in the flames for this method to work. This size change lasts 1 hour before the black troll reverts to its normal size."}],"description":"Black trolls are an offshoot of standard trolls, believed to be supernaturally altered by magic. They dwell in the same climate as their\n\nnormal brethren and often associate with them as well. Their appetites are no less impressive than other trolls, and some would argue theirs is even greater. Black trolls dine on anything they catch and kill, including scavenging and dining on the leftovers of other animals' meals. Black trolls don't eat other trolls, regardless of the food situation.\n\nBlack trolls stand 14 ft. tall and weigh around 1,000 pounds. When they swell to Huge size, they reach heights of 21 ft. or more and weigh over 3,000 pounds. Black trolls flesh is rubbery to the touch and always shiny black in color. Eyes are almost always dull gray, though a few black trolls have bright blue eyes. Young are born live and reach maturity relatively quickly. Black trolls can mate with other trolls, but the offspring is always the same type as the other parent. Only black trolls mating with their own spawn another black troll.\n\nA black troll attacks by slashing and biting its foes. Its ability to deal horrendous amounts of damage is cause for concern among many that have faced a black troll. Often when in combat, a black troll shuns fire, hoping its opponent senses a weakness and decides to unleash a fire attack at the troll. Many adventurers have met their untimely demise this way. If the ruse doesn't appear to work, and there is a large source of fire nearby, a black troll subjects itself to the fire in order to grow to Huge size.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Bonesucker","cr":7,"xp":3200,"alignment":"NE","size":"Large","type":"aberration","init":5,"senses":[{"type":"all-around vision"},{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"90 ft."}],"ac":17,"ac_touch":11,"ac_flat_footed":15,"ac_mods":"+1 Dex, +1 dodge, +6 natural, -1 size","hp":60,"hd":"8d8+24","hdvalue":8,"fort":5,"ref":5,"will":7,"dr":"10/magic","immunities":["flanking"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":20}],"melee":"4 tentacles +9 (1d4+4 plus grab and liquefy bones)","space":"10 ft.","reach":"10 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"constrict","details":"1d4+4 plus liquefy bones"}],"strength":18,"dexterity":13,"constitution":17,"intelligence":10,"wisdom":12,"charisma":13,"baseatk":6,"cmb":11,"cmb_special":"+4 vs. grapple","cmd":23,"feats":[{"feat":"Dodge"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Lightning Reflexes"},{"feat":"Skill Focus (Perception)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Climb","value":15},{"skill":"Perception","value":19},{"skill":"Stealth","value":8},{"skill":"Swim","value":15}],"languages":["Aklo"],"environments":["any land","any underground"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"standard","description_visual":"This bizarre creature resembles a fleshy tree trunk. Atop its main body protrudes a mass of writhing tentacles that constantly ooze and drip a brownish-yellow fluid. Near the top of its body is a ring of black, unblinking eyes.","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"All-Around Vision","kind":"Ex","details":"A bonesucker's symmetrically placed eyes allow it to look in any direction, bestowing a +4 racial bonus on Perception checks. Bonesuckers cannot be flanked."},{"type":"Liquefy Bones","kind":"Ex","details":"A bonesucker that has successfully grappled an opponent deals 1d2 points of Strength and 1d2 points of Dexterity damage to an opponent as long as the hold is maintained."}],"description":"A bonesucker is a bizarre creature that stalks the darkness of wastelands and dank caves. The body is encased in a thick, rubbery sheath of flesh and muscle that makes the bonesucker highly resistant to injury. The bonesucker moves about through the use of 5 thick tentacles at its base.\n\nBonesuckers consume only the bones of an opponent by grabbing it and piercing its flesh with its hollow tentacles. The tentacles inject digestive enzymes into the bones, which break down and are sucked up as a pasty meal for the bonesucker-the attack of a bonesucker is horrifyingly painful. Experienced adventurers always know they are nearing the hunting grounds of a bonesucker: the creature leaves boneless carcasses of its meals lying where it finished them.\n\nBonesuckers stand about 10 ft. tall.\n\nA bonesucker attacks with its tentacles. Initially, the tentacles appear to be only a foot or two in length, but the bonesucker can extend them to a length of approximately 10 ft. It can attack with up to four of its eight tentacles in a single round.\n\nA bonesucker's natural weapons are treated as magic weapons for the purpose of overcoming damage reduction.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Brass Man","cr":7,"xp":3200,"alignment":"N","size":"Large","type":"construct","subtypes":["extraplanar","fire"],"init":0,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"low-light vision"}],"ac":23,"ac_touch":9,"ac_flat_footed":23,"ac_mods":"+0 Dex, +14 natural, -1 size","hp":85,"hd":"10d10+30","hdvalue":10,"fort":3,"ref":3,"will":3,"dr":"10/adamantine","immunities":["construct traits","fire","magic"],"weaknesses":["vulnerability to cold"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":30}],"melee":"2 slams +15 (2d8+6), or large greatsword +15 (3d6+9)","space":"10 ft.","reach":"10 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"spit molten brass"}],"strength":23,"dexterity":10,"wisdom":11,"charisma":1,"baseatk":10,"cmb":17,"cmd":27,"environments":["any (Elemental Plane of Fire)"],"organizations":["solitary","squad (2-4)"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"This creature resembles a humanoid constructed of brass. Its features are exquisite and delicate, and ancient runes and symbols adorn its body.","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Immunity to Magic","kind":"Ex","details":"A brass man is immune to any spell or spell-like ability that allows spell resistance. In addition, certain spells and effects function differently against the creature, as noted below. A magical attack that deals electricity damage slows a brass man (as the slow spell) for 3 rounds, with no saving throw. A magical attack that deals fire damage breaks any slow effect on the brass man and heals 1 point of damage for each 3 points of damage the attack would otherwise deal. If the amount of healing would cause the brass man to exceed its full normal hit points, it gains any excess as temporary hit points. A brass man gets no saving throw against fire effects."},{"type":"Spit Molten Brass","kind":"Ex","details":"Once every 1d4 rounds (and no more than five times per day), a brass man can spit a stream of molten brass n a 30-foot line; damage 6d6 fire, Reflex half DC 15. The save DC is Constitution-based."}],"description":"Brass men are humanoid-shaped constructs built by the powerful efreet of the City of Brass. They are created for the sole purpose of guarding some efreeti secret within the walls of the City. Some are created as battle allies and aid the efreet in battle against their enemies. They are rarely encountered elsewhere, though on occasion one is sent to the Material Plane by its efreet creator to retrieve an object or creature. Brass men are very tough physical opponents and difficult to stop. Typically a brass man begins combat by spitting molten brass on the closest opponent before moving into melee where it attacks with its huge greatsword or its powerful fists. Construction The construction of the brass men is a highly guarded secret among the efreet race. No one outside the City of Brass has ever discovered the proper method of constructing a brass man, and the efreet aren't telling.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Brown Pudding","cr":7,"xp":3200,"alignment":"N","size":"Huge","type":"ooze","init":-5,"senses":[{"type":"blindsight","modifier":"60 ft."}],"ac":8,"ac_touch":3,"ac_flat_footed":8,"ac_mods":"-5 Dex, -2 size, +5 natural","hp":115,"hd":"11d8+66","hdvalue":11,"fort":9,"ref":-2,"will":-2,"defensive_abilities":["split (piercing and slashing, 10 hp)"],"immunities":["ooze traits"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":20},{"type":"climb","speed":20}],"melee":"slam +9 (2d4+4 plus 2d6 acid plus grab)","space":"15 ft.","reach":"15 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"constrict","details":"2d4+4 plus 2d6 acid"},{"type":"corrosion"}],"strength":17,"dexterity":1,"constitution":22,"wisdom":1,"charisma":1,"baseatk":8,"cmb":13,"cmb_special":"+4 vs. grapple","cmd":18,"cmd_special":"+10 vs. bull rush, can't be tripped","skills":[{"skill":"Climb","value":11}],"sq":[{"type":"suction"}],"environments":["temperate marshes","warm marshes"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"This creature appears as a large mass of undulating brown sludge.","group":"Pudding","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Acid","kind":"Ex","details":"A brown pudding secretes a digestive acid that dissolves organic material quickly, but doesn't affect metal or stone. Any melee hit or constriction attack deals acid damage, and the opponent's clothing and armor (nonmetal only) take the same amount of damage unless they succeed on DC 21 Reflex saves. A wooden weapon that strikes a brown pudding takes 2d6 acid damage unless it succeeds on a DC 21 Reflex save. If a brown pudding remains in contact with a wooden object for 1 full round, it inflicts 21 points of damage (no save) to the object. The save DCs are Constitution-based."},{"type":"Corrosion","kind":"Ex","details":"An opponent that is being constricted by a brown pudding suffers a -4 penalty on Reflex saves made to resist acid damage applying to clothing and armor."},{"type":"Suction","kind":"Ex","details":"The brown pudding can create powerful suction against any surfaces as it climbs, allowing it to cling to inverted surfaces with ease. A brown pudding can establish or release suction as a swift action, and as long as it is using suction, it moves at half speed. Because of the suction, a brown pudding's CMD score gets a +10 circumstance bonus to resist bull rush, awesome blows, and other attacks and effects that attempt to physically move it from its location."}],"description":"A variety of the black pudding, the brown pudding is found only in temperate and subtropical swamps. It is dark brown in color. Brown puddings have a tougher surface membrane than other puddings, giving them a natural armor bonus. They attack by grabbing and constricting their prey.","ecology":"","habitat_society":"","credit":"The Brown Pudding originally appeared in the First Edition module S4 Lost Caverns of Tsojcanth (© TSR/Wizards of the Coast, 1982) and later in the First Edition Monster Manual II (© TSR/Wizards of the Coast, 1983) and is used by permission."},{"name":"Burning Dervish","cr":7,"xp":3200,"alignment":"LE","size":"Medium","type":"outsider","subtypes":["extraplanar","fire"],"init":3,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."}],"ac":17,"ac_touch":14,"ac_flat_footed":13,"ac_mods":"+3 Dex, +1 dodge, +3 natural","hp":58,"hd":"9d10+9","hdvalue":9,"fort":7,"ref":6,"will":8,"immunities":["fire"],"weaknesses":["vulnerability to cold"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":30},{"type":"fly","speed":20,"maneuverability":"perfect"}],"melee":"+1 falchion +14 (2d4+7/18-20), or 2 slams +13 (1d6+4 plus 1d6 fire plus burn) (flame form only)","space":"5 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"burn","details":"1d6, DC 15"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":14,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":15,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"1/day","spells":[{"spell":"enlarge person or reduce person"},{"spell":"plane shift","details":"Elemental, Astral, or Material Planes"},{"spell":"produce flame"}]},{"frequency":"3/day","spells":[{"spell":"invisibility","details":"self only"},{"spell":"pyrotechnics"}]}],"strength":18,"dexterity":16,"constitution":13,"intelligence":13,"wisdom":15,"charisma":15,"baseatk":9,"cmb":13,"cmd":27,"feats":[{"feat":"Combat Expertise"},{"feat":"Dodge"},{"feat":"Mobility"},{"feat":"Spring Attack"},{"feat":"Whirlwind Attack"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Bluff","value":13},{"skill":"Escape Artist","value":13},{"skill":"Knowledge (planes)","value":13},{"skill":"Perception","value":14},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":13},{"skill":"Stealth","value":14},{"skill":"Survival","value":14}],"languages":["Common","Ignan","Infernal"],"sq":[{"type":"elemental endurance"},{"type":"plane shift"}],"environments":["any (Elemental Plane of Fire)","any (Plane of Molten Skies)"],"organizations":["solitary","company (2-4)","band (6-15)"],"treasure":"standard","description_visual":"This creature looks like a normal human with symbols and tattoos of alien design covering almost all of its body.","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Elemental Endurance","kind":"Ex","details":"Burning dervishes can survive on the Elemental Planes of Air or Earth for up to 48 hours and on the Elemental Plane of Water for up to 12 hours. Failure to return to the Elemental Plane of Fire or Plane of Molten Skies after that time deals 1 point of damage per hour to a burning dervish until it dies or returns to the Elemental Plane of Fire."},{"type":"Flame Form","kind":"Su","details":"Three times per day, as a standard action, a burning dervish can change its form to that of a column of fire. In this form it gains two slam attacks. The transformation lasts indefinitely; changing back requires another standard action."}],"description":"Burning dervishes are the fanatical minions of the Sultan of Efreet (see the City of Brass by Necromancer Games). It is said that the burning dervishes were once a noble tribe of jann who sold their souls to the Sultan of Efreet in exchange for greater power over the Elemental Plane of Fire.\n\nBurning dervishes are virtually indistinguishable from human beings, and indeed spend a great amount of time in the Material Plane as agents of the Sultan of Efreet, seeking to spread worship of the Sultan as true God of Elemental Fire. Other tasks of the burning dervishes are as assassins and spies, often leading daring sneak attacks against foes of the Sultan or procuring powerful relics for his pleasure.\n\nThe burning dervishes have a citadel atop the Great Ziggurat of the City of Brass which serves as the central temple to their zealous faith.\n\nIt is from this ziggurat that the Sultan communes with his worshippers, sending them out on jihads throughout the planes to further his name and power.\n\nBurning dervishes usually turn themselves invisible before attacking in an attempt to catch their foes by surprise. In combat, the burning dervish attacks with its falchion. Depending on the power of its opponent, a burning dervish either uses enlarge person on itself or reduce person on its opponent. A burning dervish that is outclassed or overmatched either takes to the air and flees or attempts to plane shift to escape.","ecology":"","habitat_society":"","gear":"+1 falchion"},{"name":"Cinder Ghoul","cr":7,"xp":3200,"alignment":"CE","size":"Large","type":"undead","subtypes":["fire"],"init":9,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."}],"ac":21,"ac_touch":15,"ac_flat_footed":15,"ac_mods":"+5 Dex, +1 dodge, +6 natural, -1 size","hp":68,"hd":"8d8+32","hdvalue":8,"fort":6,"ref":9,"will":7,"defensive_abilities":["limited gaseous form"],"dr":"10/magic","immunities":["fire","undead traits"],"weaknesses":["vulnerability to cold"],"speed":[{"type":"fly","speed":40,"maneuverability":"perfect"}],"melee":"slam +10 (1d8+4 plus 1d6 fire plus burn plus energy  drain)","space":"10 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"burn","details":"1d8, DC 18"},{"type":"energy drain","details":"1 level, DC 18"},{"type":"smoke inhalation"}],"strength":16,"dexterity":20,"intelligence":4,"wisdom":12,"charisma":19,"baseatk":6,"cmb":10,"cmd":26,"cmd_special":"can't be tripped","feats":[{"feat":"Dodge"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Lightning Reflexes"},{"feat":"Weapon Finesse"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Fly","value":18},{"skill":"Perception","value":8}],"environments":["any"],"organizations":["solitary","gang (2-5)","mob (6-11)"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"This creature is a swirling humanoid cloud of burning ash and charred body parts. A red glow of burning embers can be glimpsed floating within the mass. This creature reeks of smoke and burnt flesh.","group":"Ghoul","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Limited Gaseous Form","kind":"Ex","details":"Because it has solid body parts that constantly float and swirl within it, a cinder ghoul has a limited version of the gaseous form ability. Although other gaseous creatures can issue under the crack of a door, a cinder ghoul cannot. A cinder ghoul can, however, make slam attacks, retains its natural armor bonus, and all supernatural attacks. Spells, spell-like abilities, and supernatural abilities affect them normally. A cinder ghoul cannot enter water or other liquid. It isn't ethereal or incorporeal, and is affected by winds or other forms of moving air to the extent that the wind pushes them in the direction the wind is moving. However, even the strongest wind can't disperse or damage a cinder ghoul. Because it contains burning embers and small bits of perpetually smoldering flesh, a cinder ghoul cannot hide and gets no bonuses to Stealth checks in an area of mist, smoke, or other gas."},{"type":"Smoke Inhalation","kind":"Su","details":"As a standard action, a cinder ghoul can attempt to force some of its smoky form into the lungs of a living opponent. To initiate this attack it must move into its target's space. The target must then make a successful DC 18 Fortitude save or inhale part of the creature. Smoke inside the victim's lungs burns the surrounding tissues and organs, dealing 1d2 points of Constitution damage each round. The affected creature can attempt another Fortitude save each round to cough out the burning residue. The save DC is Charisma-based."}],"description":"A creature that is burned to death by magical fire may rise again as a fiery undead being called a cinder ghoul. The lairs of old red dragons may be haunted by many of these pathetic, angry spirits, and many a wizard that has dispatched a foe with a well-placed fireball has been found mysteriously charred to death many months after the deed.\n\nCinder ghouls are barely intelligent, but they do have a very vivid recollection of the pain they endured in the moments before their death.\n\nFilled with anger as fiery as the flames that took their life, cinder ghouls harbor a strong hatred of fire and any living creature that has control over it.\n\nAlthough it cannot speak, the sound of wailing and screaming and the rushing of fire-stoked wind constantly accompany a cinder ghoul.\n\nIn melee a cinder ghoul slams with the charred remains of its fists. If a cinder ghoul encounters an opponent that demonstrates any form of control over fire-either through casting a fire spell or using a magic item that produces fire-it attacks that opponent to the exclusion of all others.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Dire Smilodon","cr":7,"xp":3200,"alignment":"N","size":"Large","type":"animal","init":3,"senses":[{"type":"low-light vision"}],"ac":20,"ac_touch":12,"ac_flat_footed":17,"ac_mods":"+3 Dex, +8 natural, -1 size","hp":112,"hd":"9d8+72","hdvalue":9,"fort":14,"ref":9,"will":3,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":50}],"melee":"bite +15 (2d6+10/19-20 plus grab plus bleed), 2 claws  +15 (1d6+10 plus grab)","space":"10 ft.","reach":"10 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"bleed","details":"1d3"},{"type":"pounce"},{"type":"rake","details":"2 claws +15, 1d6+10"}],"strength":31,"dexterity":17,"constitution":27,"intelligence":2,"wisdom":16,"charisma":10,"baseatk":6,"cmb":9,"cmd":23,"cmd_special":"+4 vs. trip","feats":[{"feat":"Improved Critical (bite)"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Run"},{"feat":"Skill Focus (Perception)"},{"feat":"Skill Focus (Stealth)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Acrobatics","value":12},{"skill":"Perception","value":13},{"skill":"Stealth","value":11,"special":"+15 in heavy undergrowth or tall grass"},{"skill":"Swim","value":14}],"environments":["any plains","warm forests"],"organizations":["solitary","pair","den (6-10)"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"With fangs like swords, this cat's gleaming eyes and wicked claws promise death to anything it sees as prey.","group":"Smilodon","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Dragon Horse","cr":7,"xp":3200,"alignment":"NG","size":"Large","type":"magical beast","subtypes":["air"],"init":7,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"low-light vision"}],"ac":21,"ac_touch":13,"ac_flat_footed":18,"ac_mods":"+3 Dex, +8 natural","hp":76,"hd":"8d10+32","hdvalue":8,"fort":10,"ref":9,"will":8,"sr":16,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":60},{"type":"fly","speed":120,"maneuverability":"good"}],"melee":"2 hooves +14 (1d6+7)","space":"10 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"breath weapon","details":"30 ft. cone, DC 18, 8d6 cold, usable once every 10 rounds"},{"type":"flying charge"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":11,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":15,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"detect chaos"},{"spell":"detect evil"},{"spell":"detect good"},{"spell":"detect law"}]},{"frequency":"1/minute","spells":[{"spell":"fog cloud","details":"CL 8th"},{"spell":"gust of wind","details":"CL 8th"}]},{"frequency":"3/day","spells":[{"spell":"plane shift"}]}],"strength":24,"dexterity":17,"constitution":19,"intelligence":16,"wisdom":18,"charisma":20,"baseatk":8,"cmb":16,"cmd":29,"cmd_special":"+4 vs. trip","feats":[{"feat":"Flyby Attack"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Power Attack"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Fly","value":16},{"skill":"Knowledge (planes)","value":11},{"skill":"Perception","value":19},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":12},{"skill":"Survival","value":12}],"languages":["Common","Draconic","Auran","telepathy 100 ft."],"environments":["any"],"organizations":["solitary","family (2-3)"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"This creature resembles a horse with a smooth coat of scintillating blue hues that seem to flicker and wash over its body in waves as it gallops through the air. Its deep sky blue hooves don't touch the ground as it moves. The mane and tail of a dragon horse is of purest white and flows out behind it in an elegant cascade.","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Breath Weapon","kind":"Su","details":"A dragon horse's breath weapon is a 30 ft. cone of cold. It can only use its breath weapon once every 10 rounds (1/minute)."},{"type":"Flying Charge","kind":"Ex","details":"A dragon horse gains a +2 bonus on damage rolls if it charges while flying."},{"type":"Plane Shift","kind":"Sp","details":"A dragon horse can enter the Ethereal Plane, Astral Plane, Elemental Plane of Air, or the Material Plane. This ability transports the dragon horse and up to two other creatures, provided they are on its back."}],"description":"Dragon horses are beautiful, graceful creatures, peaceful and reclusive.\n\nThey spend nearly all their time aloft among the clouds, rarely deigning to set foot on solid ground. Being peaceful creatures, dragon horses dislike combat and seek to avoid it, unless pressed. In melee, a dragon horse attempts to deal nonlethal damage to its opponents. Unconscious opponents are not further attacked.\n\nThe name \"dragon horse\" is something of a misnomer, as these creatures have no relation to true dragons. They are, in fact, more closely related to the noble ki-rin. Dragon horses are creatures originally from the Elemental Plane of Air that have decided, for reasons unknown to anyone but themselves, to reside more or less permanently in the Material Plane.\n\nDragon horses visit the Elemental Plane of Air frequently, however.\n\nDragon horses are solitary creatures, but a mated pair will often remain together to raise their young. They have no need or desire for material possessions and so keep no treasure.\n\nTraining a Dragon Horse Dragon horses are highly prized as steeds, but they are notoriously difficult to train. They have a very free spirit and don't tolerate captivity, thus only juvenile dragon horses have any chance of being tamed mounts.\n\nDragon horse foals have the Young template, and mature to adult size after 10 years. A captive foal can be raised only by a good being and doing so requires 10 years and a Handle Animal check (DC 30) every 6 months.","ecology":"","habitat_society":"","credit":"The Dragon Horse originally appeared in the First Edition Monster Manual II (© TSR/Wizards of the Coast, 1983) and is used by permission."}];
